        d.numbered([f'**Delivery payments are collected before handover.** The models collect them at project months 30 (Green Square) and 45 (L\'avenir), 18 and 9 months before handover. If collected at handover the peak shortages are EGP {fmt(G["fund"]["stress_peak"],0)} and {fmt(L["fund"]["stress_peak"],0)} million, not EGP {fmt(G["fund"]["model_peak"],1)} and {fmt(L["fund"]["model_peak"],1)} million.',
                    f'**Price growth.** The plans need list prices to rise {gp(G)[0]*100:.0f}% and {gp(G)[1]*100:.0f}% (Green Square retail, offices) and {gp(L)[0]*100:.0f}% and {gp(L)[1]*100:.0f}% (L\'avenir); launch office prices exceed current Mostakbal City asking prices; recent growth evidence is mixed.', f'**Sellable office area** exceeds office built-up area in both projects; not yet reconciled.',
                    '**Cost basis.** Construction cost is a stage schedule multiplied by a factor of 8 that is not yet explained; no inflation; no separate pre-construction cost.', '**No sales are contracted yet** and the permit, title and consent documents in sections 2 and 3 are provided after the investor signs the non-disclosure agreement.',
                    f'**Payout coverage.** Net cash flow covers Option B instalments by 1.5x or more in only {G["B"]["S"]["S1"]["res"]["Base"]["n"]-G["B"]["S"]["S1"]["res"]["Base"]["strict_below"]} of {G["B"]["S"]["S1"]["res"]["Base"]["n"]} quarters in Green Square and {L["B"]["S"]["S1"]["res"]["Base"]["n"]-L["B"]["S"]["S1"]["res"]["Base"]["strict_below"]} of {L["B"]["S"]["S1"]["res"]["Base"]["n"]} in L\'avenir. Pooled cash covers at least {mx(min(G["B"]["S"]["S1"]["res"]["Base"]["liq_min"], L["B"]["S"]["S1"]["res"]["Base"]["liq_min"]),1)} in the base case.',
                    f'**Downside funding need.** With sales delayed 12 months and prices 10% lower the funding needs are EGP {fmt(G["fund"]["downside_peak"],0)} and {fmt(L["fund"]["downside_peak"],0)} million, EGP {fmt(-S["Downside: sales +12 months, prices -10%"]["comb_peak"],0)} million together, and the lowest combined pooled cash after Option B payouts is EGP {fmt(S1["Downside"]["min_cash"],0)} million. The investor relies on Jalour\'s capacity to fund it; there is no parent guarantee and no restricted account.',
                    f'**Both projects are short at the same time in stress cases.** The combined base-case low is EGP {fmt(-sp["comb_min"],1)} million in month {sp["comb_min_m"]}; the funding undertaking draws on Jalour\'s cash reserves and on other projects\' cash outside these two, which are not shown.',
                    f'**Option A uses the first sales tranches.** The investor receives {pct(G["A"]["f"],0)} (Green Square) and {pct(L["A"]["f"],0)} (L\'avenir) of the launch-priced inventory, which raises the peak shortage before the ticket to EGP {fmt(-G["A"]["jal"]["peak_ex_ticket"],1)} and {fmt(-L["A"]["jal"]["peak_ex_ticket"],1)} million and gives the investor units that compete with Jalour\'s later sales.', '**Commission timing.** The models pay commission 12 months after each sale quarter; if paid at sale, early funding needs are higher.',
                    '**Sponsor information** (track record, audited accounts) is provided only after the investor signs the non-disclosure agreement, and the **form of the investor\'s instrument** is still open.', '**Market data** are reported from third-party summaries and asking prices; they are not audited.'])
